 "A step-by-step process to regulate your system and reconnect with yourself.": "",
 "layer by layer": "",
 "The Breathwork Way is a breathwork-centered framework that brings together nervous system regulation and somatic depth that I often describe it with an onion. <br>Over the years we all build up layers: habits, tension, protective patterns, emotions we never had time for, each one is there for a reason.": "",
 "<b>So we never go straight for the core </b>but we start from the outside and move inward, one layer at a time listening to what your body shows us and what it is ready for.": "",
 "I use this framework with the clients I work with in Lisbon and online.": "",
 "<span><i></i>Regulate</span> <span><i></i>Reveal</span> <span><i></i>Release</span>": "",
 "Layer 01 · Stabilize": "",
 "Everything starts with knowing where you are.": "",
 "We begin with an assessment of your nervous system: how you respond to stress, where you tend to get stuck and what your breath is already telling us.": "",
 "If you've been running on high alert for a long time, this is where your system can finally start to settle. Together we find the practices and resources that work for you, so you always have a way back to calm and back to yourself when life gets stressful.": "",
 "<b>Nervous system assessment</b><em>Understanding where you are and your nervous system's baseline capacity.</em>": "",
 "<b>Breathing mechanics</b><em>Finding your natural, functional breathing pattern and optimising how you breathe.</em>": "",
 "<b>Pattern recognition</b><em>Identifying how you respond to stress and building resources to come back to calm and control.</em>": "",
 "Layer 02 · Understand": "",
 "Breathwork as psychological archaeology.": "",
 "Once you feel safer in your body, we can start exploring what's underneath. Tension, sensations and recurring symptoms are often your body's way of communicating, and here we use them as our guide.": "",
 "This is often where we meet parts of you that have been carrying a story or an emotion for a long time. We approach them with curiosity and care, at your pace, building a real connection with your body and what it has been trying to tell you.": "",
 "<b>Somatic exploration</b><em>Using sensations and tension as a doorway to find where emotions and stories are held.</em>": "",
 "<b>Inner connection</b><em>Meeting the parts of you that carry a story and establishing a dialogue with them.</em>": "",
 "<b>Protective role identification</b><em>Understanding the unconscious strategies that hold you back.</em>": "",
 "Layer 03 · Transform": "",
 "Trusting the wisdom of the breath.": "",
 "In this phase we move beyond the conscious mind. Through breathwork, we access the subconscious, where so much of what we carry is stored.": "",
 "Here the thinking mind can rest and the breath leads the way. Whatever comes up in each session is what you're ready to see and work on.": "",
 "<b>Breathwork journeys</b><em>Conscious connected breathing to reach deeper layers.</em>": "",
 "<b>Layered release</b><em>Working gently, in a trauma-informed way, one layer at a time.</em>": "",
 "<b>Nervous system completion</b><em>Allowing stored stress cycles to complete.</em>": "",
